    "title": "Symmetric Rank-1 (SR1) Update",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-802\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"120\" y=\"16\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">SR1:  B\u2096\u208a\u2081 = B\u2096 + r r\u1d40 / r\u1d40s\u2096,   r = y\u2096 \u2212 B\u2096s\u2096</text><rect x=\"62.0\" y=\"46\" width=\"20.0\" height=\"26\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"72.0\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">B\u2096</text><text x=\"72.0\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">old curvature</text><text x=\"72.0\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">model</text><text x=\"91.0\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">+</text><rect x=\"100.0\" y=\"46\" width=\"30.0\" height=\"26\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"115.0\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">r r\u1d40</text><text x=\"115.0\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">one correction,</text><text x=\"115.0\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">only along r</text><text x=\"139.0\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">/</text><rect x=\"148.0\" y=\"46\" width=\"30.0\" height=\"26\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"163.0\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">r\u1d40s\u2096</text><text x=\"163.0\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">scale so that</text><text x=\"163.0\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">B\u2096\u208a\u2081s\u2096 = y\u2096</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">r = y\u2096 \u2212 B\u2096s\u2096: how far the old model misses the secant</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">r\u1d40s\u2096 \u2248 0: dividing by ~0, so skip this update</text><g transform=\"translate(224.0 14.0) rotate(0) scale(0.45)\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polygon points=\"12,0 5,-2.2 -9,-1.6 -9,1.6 5,2.2\"/><polygon points=\"3,0 -4,-10 -7,-10 -3,0 -7,10 -4,10\"/><polygon points=\"-8,0 -11,-4.5 -12.5,-4.5 -10.5,0 -12.5,4.5 -11,4.5\"/></g></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "SR1 measures the miss r = y\u2096 \u2212 B\u2096s\u2096 (what the old model predicts for the hop versus what the slope really did) and adds one rank-1 correction r r\u1d40 / r\u1d40s\u2096 along it, which makes B\u2096\u208a\u2081s\u2096 = y\u2096. If r\u1d40s\u2096 is nearly zero the update is skipped.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Unique Rank-1 Form:</strong> If we seek a symmetric rank-1 update $B_{k+1} = B_k + c u u^T$ satisfying the secant equation, there is <strong>EXACTLY ONE</strong> unique mathematical solution: the SR1 update.",
      "<strong>Key Strength:</strong> Remarkably, on quadratics, SR1 generates true Hessian approximations even with ARBITRARY step sizes (no line search required)!",
      "<strong>Fatal Flaw:</strong> The denominator $(y_k - B_k s_k)^T s_k$ can vanish or become negative. SR1 does NOT guarantee positive definiteness ($B_{k+1} \\succ 0$), making it unstable for standard line search."
    ],
    "math": "$$B_{k+1} = B_k + \\frac{(y_k - B_k s_k)(y_k - B_k s_k)^T}{(y_k - B_k s_k)^T s_k}, \\quad H_{k+1} = H_k + \\frac{(s_k - H_k y_k)(s_k - H_k y_k)^T}{(s_k - H_k y_k)^T y_k}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The airplane analogy.</strong> A single rank-one correction to the curvature estimate: quick and light, but if the denominator is near zero the update can blow up and the estimate jams.",
    "examTrap": "Never use SR1 with line search without a skip check! Production SR1 codes skip the update whenever $|s_k^T (y_k - B_k s_k)| < r \\|s_k\\| \\|y_k - B_k s_k\\|$, and pair it with Trust Region frameworks.",
    "hint": "What is the cheapest possible correction that still satisfies the secant equation?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$y_k-B_ks_k$ = the error:</strong> what the old estimate failed to predict about the slope change.",
      "<strong>$vv^\\top/(v^\\top s)$ with $v=y_k-B_ks_k$</strong> adds a correction in exactly that direction, a rank-one update.",
      "<strong>The denominator $(y_k-B_ks_k)^\\top s_k$</strong> rescales it so the secant equation holds; if it is near 0 the update blows up."
    ],
