    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-1005\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M118.0,76.0 L59.7,54.8 L56.9,65.2 L56.0,76.0 L56.9,86.8 L59.7,97.2 L64.3,107.0 L70.5,115.9 L78.1,123.5 L87.0,129.7 L96.8,134.3 L107.2,137.1 L118.0,138.0 L128.8,137.1\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M118.0,76.0 L170.6,95.2 L173.3,84.9 L174.0,74.4 L172.7,63.9 L169.4,53.8 L164.3,44.6 L157.6,36.4 L149.4,29.7 L140.2,24.6 L130.1,21.3 L119.6,20.0 L109.1,20.7 L98.8,23.4\" fill=\"#eef0f4\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 3\"/><path d=\"M118.0,76.0 L163.3,68.0 L162.4,64.1 L161.2,60.3 L159.7,56.6 L157.8,53.0 L155.7,49.6 L153.2,46.4 L150.5,43.5 L147.6,40.8 L144.4,38.3 L141.0,36.2 L137.4,34.3 L133.7,32.8\" fill=\"#c9ced8\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><g transform=\"translate(118.0 76.0) rotate(-40) scale(0.7)\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polygon points=\"12,0 5,-2.2 -9,-1.6 -9,1.6 5,2.2\"/><polygon points=\"3,0 -4,-10 -7,-10 -3,0 -7,10 -4,10\"/><polygon points=\"-8,0 -11,-4.5 -12.5,-4.5 -10.5,0 -12.5,4.5 -11,4.5\"/></g><text x=\"141.7\" y=\"56.1\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"serif\" font-style=\"italic\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">K</text><text x=\"183.4\" y=\"85.2\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-family=\"serif\" font-style=\"italic\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">K*</text><text x=\"89.8\" y=\"101.4\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-family=\"serif\" font-style=\"italic\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">K\u00b0</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\"> </text><text x=\"8\" y=\"16\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">K* = {y : y\u1d40x \u2265 0 for all x \u2208 K}</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">K\u00b0 = \u2212K*</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The dual cone K* holds every y making a non-obtuse angle with all of K: y\u1d40x \u2265 0 for every x \u2208 K. The polar cone is its mirror, K\u00b0 = \u2212K*. Taking the dual twice gives K back exactly when K is closed and convex.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Dual Cone $K^*$:</strong> For any cone $K \\subset \\mathbb{R}^n$, its dual cone is: $K^* = \\{y \\in \\mathbb{R}^n : y^T x \\ge 0, \\; \\forall x \\in K\\}$. It is always convex and closed, even if $K$ is neither!",
      "<strong>Polar Cone $K^\\circ$:</strong> Defined by negative inner products: $K^\\circ = \\{y \\in \\mathbb{R}^n : y^T x \\le 0, \\; \\forall x \\in K\\} = -K^*$.",
      "<strong>Bipolar Theorem:</strong> For any closed convex cone $K$, the double dual recovers the original cone: $(K^*)^* = K$ and $(K^\\circ)^\\circ = K$."
    ],
    "math": "$$K^* = \\{y : y^\\top  x \\ge 0 \\, \\forall x \\in K\\}, \\quad (K^*)^* = K \\iff K \\text{ is closed and convex}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The airplane analogy.</strong> The legal headings from your parking spot form a cone $K$. The polar cone $K^\\circ$ is the set of 'gravity pulls' that make every legal heading go uphill or flat: pulls that can never make the plane roll anywhere legal. At a minimum, $-\\nabla f$ must lie in $K^\\circ$.",
    "examTrap": "Self-dual cones: The non-negative orthant $\\mathbb{R}_+^n$ and the cone of positive semidefinite matrices $\\mathbb{S}_+^n$ are strictly <strong>self-dual</strong> ($K^* = K$).",
    "hint": "Which pulls can never make a legal heading go downhill?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$K^*=\\{y:y^\\top x\\ge0\\ \\forall x\\in K\\}$:</strong> forces that never oppose any legal heading.",
      "<strong>The polar cone $K^\\circ=-K^*$</strong> is the set of pulls that make every legal heading go flat or uphill: at a minimum, $-\\nabla f\\in K^\\circ$.",
      "<strong>$(K^*)^*=K$ for closed convex $K$:</strong> taking the dual twice gets the original cone back."
    ],
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "For a cone $K$, the <b>dual cone</b> is $K^*=\\{y: y^\\top x\\ge0\\ \\forall x\\in K\\}$ and the <b>polar cone</b> is $K^\\circ=\\{y: y^\\top x\\le0\\ \\forall x\\in K\\}=-K^*$. For a closed convex cone, $K^{**}=K$.",
    "textbookImg": null,
