    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-1103\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M32.0,32.0 L36.4,39.8 L40.8,47.2 L45.2,54.2 L49.6,60.8 L54.0,67.0 L58.4,72.8 L62.8,78.2 L67.2,83.2 L71.6,87.8 L76.0,92.0 L80.4,95.8 L84.8,99.2 L89.2,102.2 L93.6,104.8 L98.0,107.0 L102.4,108.8 L106.8,110.2 L111.2,111.2 L115.6,111.8 L120.0,112.0 L124.4,111.8 L128.8,111.2 L133.2,110.2 L137.6,108.8 L142.0,107.0 L146.4,104.8 L150.8,102.2 L155.2,99.2 L159.6,95.8 L164.0,92.0 L168.4,87.8 L172.8,83.2 L177.2,78.2 L181.6,72.8 L186.0,67.0 L190.4,60.8 L194.8,54.2 L199.2,47.2 L203.6,39.8 L208.0,32.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"32.0\" y1=\"28.0\" x2=\"32.0\" y2=\"112.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"32.0\" y1=\"35.0\" x2=\"26.0\" y2=\"35.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"32.0\" y1=\"49.0\" x2=\"26.0\" y2=\"49.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"32.0\" y1=\"63.0\" x2=\"26.0\" y2=\"63.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"32.0\" y1=\"77.0\" x2=\"26.0\" y2=\"77.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"32.0\" y1=\"91.0\" x2=\"26.0\" y2=\"91.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"32.0\" y1=\"105.0\" x2=\"26.0\" y2=\"105.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"208.0\" y1=\"28.0\" x2=\"208.0\" y2=\"112.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"208.0\" y1=\"35.0\" x2=\"214.0\" y2=\"35.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"208.0\" y1=\"49.0\" x2=\"214.0\" y2=\"49.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"208.0\" y1=\"63.0\" x2=\"214.0\" y2=\"63.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"208.0\" y1=\"77.0\" x2=\"214.0\" y2=\"77.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"208.0\" y1=\"91.0\" x2=\"214.0\" y2=\"91.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"208.0\" y1=\"105.0\" x2=\"214.0\" y2=\"105.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><g transform=\"translate(120.0 94.0) rotate(0) scale(1)\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polygon points=\"12,0 5,-2.2 -9,-1.6 -9,1.6 5,2.2\"/><polygon points=\"3,0 -4,-10 -7,-10 -3,0 -7,10 -4,10\"/><polygon points=\"-8,0 -11,-4.5 -12.5,-4.5 -10.5,0 -12.5,4.5 -11,4.5\"/></g><line x1=\"66.0\" y1=\"112.0\" x2=\"174.0\" y2=\"112.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"120.0\" cy=\"112.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"serif\" font-style=\"italic\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">x*: global min</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"16\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f, g\u2c7c convex, h\u1d62 affine</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">KKT \u21d2 f(x*) \u2264 f(x) for all x \u2208 \u03a9</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "In a convex valley (f and every g\u2c7c convex) with flat equality walls (h\u1d62 affine), any KKT point is a global minimum: f(x*) \u2264 f(x) for every legal x.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Master Sufficiency Theorem:</strong> Suppose $f(x)$ and all inequality constraints $g_j(x)$ are convex functions, and all equality constraints $h_i(x) = a_i^\\top x - b_i$ are affine.",
      "If $(x^*, \\lambda^*, \\mu^*)$ satisfies the 4 KKT conditions, then $x^*$ is an <strong>absolute global minimizer</strong> of the constrained optimization problem!",
      "<strong>Proof:</strong> Since $\\mu_j^* \\ge 0$, $\\mathcal{L}(x, \\lambda^*, \\mu^*)$ is convex in $x$. Stationarity $\\nabla_x \\mathcal{L} = 0$ makes $x^*$ a global minimizer of $\\mathcal{L}$. Complementary slackness then sandwiches $f(x^*) \\le \\mathcal{L}(x^*, \\lambda^*, \\mu^*) \\le \\mathcal{L}(x, \\lambda^*, \\mu^*) \\le f(x)$."
    ],
    "math": "$$f, g_j \\text{ convex}, \\, h_i \\text{ affine}, \\, (x^*, \\lambda^*, \\mu^*) \\in \\text{KKT} \\implies f(x^*) \\le f(x) \\; \\forall \\, x \\in \\Omega$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The airplane analogy.</strong> In a convex valley with flat walls there is only one lowest parking spot. If you are parked where the wall pushes cancel gravity (KKT holds), no deeper valley exists anywhere else in the legal airspace, so this stationary spot is already the global minimum.",
    "examTrap": "Equality constraints $h_i(x) = 0$ MUST be AFFINE ($A x = b$)! If an equality constraint is non-linear (even if $h_i$ is convex), the feasible set $\\{x : h_i(x) = 0\\}$ is NOT convex, and KKT sufficiency fails.",
    "hint": "When does a balanced parking spot have to be the global lowest one?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$f,g_j$ convex and $h_i$ affine:</strong> a convex valley with convex airspace.",
      "<strong>KKT then says a balanced point</strong> beats every other legal point: $f(x^*)\\le f(x)$.",
      "<strong>It works because the tangent plane at $x^*$ lies under the terrain,</strong> and the wall pushes cannot make it better."
    ],
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>KKT sufficiency.</b> If $f$ and every $g_j$ are convex, every $h_i$ is affine, and $(x^*,\\lambda,\\mu)$ satisfies the KKT conditions, then $x^*$ is a global minimizer.",
