    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-1106\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><clipPath id=\"cl1106\"><rect x=\"20\" y=\"10\" width=\"130\" height=\"108\"/></clipPath><polygon points=\"20,12 126,118 20,118\" fill=\"#e5e7eb\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"98\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"98\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-1106)\"/><line x1=\"34\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"34\" y2=\"10\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-1106)\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"126\" y2=\"118\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><g clip-path=\"url(#cl1106)\"><ellipse cx=\"34\" cy=\"98\" rx=\"32.19937887599697\" ry=\"16.099689437998485\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\" transform=\"rotate(0 34 98)\"/><ellipse cx=\"34\" cy=\"98\" rx=\"64.39875775199394\" ry=\"32.19937887599697\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" transform=\"rotate(0 34 98)\"/><ellipse cx=\"34\" cy=\"98\" rx=\"96.59813662799091\" ry=\"48.299068313995456\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\" transform=\"rotate(0 34 98)\"/></g><circle cx=\"34.0\" cy=\"98.0\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">O</text><line x1=\"91.6\" y1=\"83.6\" x2=\"69.6\" y2=\"105.6\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-1106)\"/><text x=\"67.6\" y=\"113.6\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2212\u2207f</text><line x1=\"70.0\" y1=\"62.0\" x2=\"56.0\" y2=\"76.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-1106)\"/><text x=\"54.0\" y=\"66.0\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2207g</text><circle cx=\"91.6\" cy=\"83.6\" r=\"2.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><g transform=\"translate(100.6 74.6) rotate(135) scale(0.55)\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polygon points=\"12,0 5,-2.2 -9,-1.6 -9,1.6 5,2.2\"/><polygon points=\"3,0 -4,-10 -7,-10 -3,0 -7,10 -4,10\"/><polygon points=\"-8,0 -11,-4.5 -12.5,-4.5 -10.5,0 -12.5,4.5 -11,4.5\"/></g><text x=\"148\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2081</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2082</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f = x\u2081\u00b2 + 4x\u2082\u00b2</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">(ovals = level sets)</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">g = 1 \u2212 x\u2081 \u2212 x\u2082 \u2264 0</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">wall: x\u2081 + x\u2082 = 1</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">x* = (4/5, 1/5)</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc* = 8/5 > 0 \u2713</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">O: g = 1 > 0 \u2717</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Case 2: oval f = 4/5 just touches the wall</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Drawn to scale. The ovals are level sets of f = x\u2081\u00b2 + 4x\u2082\u00b2. The shaded side of the line x\u2081 + x\u2082 = 1 is illegal (g > 0) and contains the origin, the Case 1 answer. The oval f = 4/5 just touches the wall at x* = (4/5, 1/5), where \u2212\u2207f = (8/5)\u2207g.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Problem:</strong> Minimize $f(x) = x_1^2 + 4 x_2^2$ subject to $g(x) = 1 - x_1 - x_2 \\le 0$.",
      "<strong>Case 1 (Inactive, $\\mu = 0$):</strong> $\\nabla f(x) = [2 x_1, 8 x_2]^T = [0, 0]^T \\implies x = (0, 0)$. Check feasibility: $g(0, 0) = 1 > 0$ $\\implies$ <strong>INFEASIBLE!</strong> Reject Case 1.",
      "<strong>Case 2 (Active, $g(x) = 0$):</strong> $x_1 + x_2 = 1$. Stationarity: $2 x_1 - \\mu = 0$ and $8 x_2 - \\mu = 0 \\implies x_1 = \\mu/2, x_2 = \\mu/8$. Substitute: $\\frac{\\mu}{2} + \\frac{\\mu}{8} = 1 \\implies \\frac{5\\mu}{8} = 1 \\implies \\mu^* = 8/5 > 0$. Point $x^* = (4/5, 1/5)$. Both dual feasibility and complementary slackness hold!"
    ],
    "math": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\mu=0:&\\ \\nabla f=(2x_1,8x_2)=0\\Rightarrow x=(0,0),\\ g(0,0)=1\\gt0\\ \\times\\\\ g=0:&\\ 2x_1-\\mu=0,\\ 8x_2-\\mu=0,\\ x_1+x_2=1\\Rightarrow\\tfrac{5\\mu}{8}=1\\\\ &\\mu^*=\\tfrac85\\gt0,\\ \\ x^*=\\left(\\tfrac45,\\tfrac15\\right),\\ \\ f(x^*)=\\tfrac45\\ \\checkmark\\end{aligned}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The airplane analogy.</strong> Case analysis is the pilot's two guesses. Case 1: assume you are floating free in the open (wall push $\\mu=0$); if the lowest open-air point lies outside legal airspace, that guess is dead. Case 2: assume you are pressed against the wall; solving the force balance gives a positive push $\\mu=8/5$, so the guess is consistent.",
    "examTrap": "When solving KKT by cases, NEVER stop upon finding a solution! You must verify dual feasibility ($\\mu_j \\ge 0$) and check if any other active sets could also satisfy KKT.",
    "hint": "Which of the two guesses survives: floating free or pressed to the wall?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>Case $\\mu=0$:</strong> with the wall switched off, $\\nabla f=0$ puts you at the origin, but $g(0,0)=1\\gt0$ breaks the constraint, so this case is rejected.",
      "<strong>Case $g=0$:</strong> stationarity $\\nabla f+\\mu\\nabla g=0$ gives $x_1=\\mu/2$ and $x_2=\\mu/8$; putting them on the wall $x_1+x_2=1$ gives $\\mu^*=8/5$ and $x^*=(4/5,1/5)$.",
      "<strong>Check:</strong> $\\mu^*\\gt0$ (dual feasibility), $g(x^*)=0$ (primal feasibility and complementary slackness), and $f$ is convex, so $x^*$ is the global minimum."
    ],
    "textbookImg": null,
    "textbookRef": null,
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Question.</b> Minimize $f(x)=x_1^2+4x_2^2$ subject to $g(x)=1-x_1-x_2\\le0$. Find the KKT point by trying the two active sets: wall inactive ($\\mu=0$) and wall active ($g=0$)."
