    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-1304\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M128.0,106.0 L191.0,94.9 L189.8,89.4 L188.1,84.1 L186.0,79.0 L183.4,74.0 L180.4,69.3 L177.0,64.9 L173.3,60.7 L169.1,57.0 L164.7,53.6 L160.0,50.6 L155.0,48.0 L149.9,45.9\" fill=\"#c9ced8\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M128.0,106.0 L79.1,88.2 L76.8,97.0 L76.0,106.0 L76.8,115.0 L79.1,123.8 L83.0,132.0 L88.2,139.4 L94.6,145.8 L102.0,151.0 L110.2,154.9 L119.0,157.2 L128.0,158.0 L137.0,157.2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"128.0\" y1=\"106.0\" x2=\"88.0\" y2=\"36.7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-1304)\"/><text x=\"84\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"serif\" font-style=\"italic\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><line x1=\"128.0\" y1=\"106.0\" x2=\"145.6\" y2=\"57.7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-1304)\"/><text x=\"152\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"serif\" font-style=\"italic\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">P\u1d0b(x)</text><line x1=\"128.0\" y1=\"106.0\" x2=\"70.4\" y2=\"85.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-1304)\"/><text x=\"68\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"serif\" font-style=\"italic\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">P\u1d0b\u00b0(x)</text><line x1=\"88.0\" y1=\"36.7\" x2=\"145.6\" y2=\"57.7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 3\"/><line x1=\"88.0\" y1=\"36.7\" x2=\"70.4\" y2=\"85.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 3\"/><g transform=\"translate(128.0 106.0) rotate(-40) scale(0.6)\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polygon points=\"12,0 5,-2.2 -9,-1.6 -9,1.6 5,2.2\"/><polygon points=\"3,0 -4,-10 -7,-10 -3,0 -7,10 -4,10\"/><polygon points=\"-8,0 -11,-4.5 -12.5,-4.5 -10.5,0 -12.5,4.5 -11,4.5\"/></g><text x=\"108\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">x = P\u1d0b(x) + P\u1d0b\u00b0(x)</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">K</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">K\u00b0</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Moreau: any x splits into a part P\u1d0b(x) in the cone K and a part P\u1d0b\u00b0(x) in its polar cone, x = P\u1d0b(x) + P\u1d0b\u00b0(x), and the two parts are perpendicular: P\u1d0b(x)\u1d40P\u1d0b\u00b0(x) = 0.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>What:</strong> for a closed convex cone $K$ and its polar cone $K^\\circ$, every vector splits uniquely into $x=\\Pi_K(x)+\\Pi_{K^\\circ}(x)$ with the two pieces perpendicular.",
      "<strong>How:</strong> the polar cone $K^\\circ=\\{y:\\langle y,x\\rangle\\le0\\ \\forall x\\in K\\}$ is the set of vectors at an obtuse (or right) angle to everything in $K$. The pieces satisfy $\\langle\\Pi_K(x),\\Pi_{K^\\circ}(x)\\rangle=0$.",
      "<strong>Why it matters:</strong> it generalizes the split of $\\mathbb{R}^n$ into a subspace plus its orthogonal complement to cones. In 1-D it is just $x=\\max(0,x)+\\min(0,x)$."
    ],
    "math": "$$x=P_K(x)+P_{K^\\circ}(x),\\qquad P_K(x)^\\top P_{K^\\circ}(x)=0$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The airplane analogy.</strong> Any wind vector splits into a part pointing inside the legal cone ($K$) and a part pointing out of it (the polar cone $K^\\circ$), and the two parts are perpendicular. One way of resolving wind into 'with the airspace' and 'against the wall' is the Moreau decomposition, like $x=x_++x_-$ in one dimension.",
    "examTrap": "Moreau's decomposition holds ONLY for CONES (sets closed under positive scaling $\\alpha K \\subseteq K$ for $\\alpha \\ge 0$). It does NOT hold for arbitrary bounded convex sets like boxes or balls!",
    "hint": "How does Moreau split any wind vector into 'with the airspace' and 'against the wall'?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$P_K(x)\\in K$:</strong> the part that points into the legal cone.",
      "<strong>$P_{K^\\circ}(x)\\in K^\\circ$:</strong> the part that points out of it.",
      "<strong>$P_K(x)^\\top P_{K^\\circ}(x)=0$:</strong> the two parts are perpendicular; in 1D this is $x=x_++x_-$."
    ],
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Moreau decomposition.</b> Let $K$ be a closed convex cone with polar $K^\\circ$. Every $x$ can be written uniquely as $x=P_K(x)+P_{K^\\circ}(x)$ with $P_K(x)^\\top P_{K^\\circ}(x)=0$.",
