    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-1306\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"30\" y=\"32\" width=\"24\" height=\"90\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"32\" width=\"24\" height=\"45\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#c9ced8\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"62\" y=\"62\" width=\"24\" height=\"60\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"62\" y=\"62\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#c9ced8\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"94\" y=\"92\" width=\"24\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"126\" y=\"110\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"77\" x2=\"158\" y2=\"77\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 3\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c4 = 0.75</text><line x1=\"14\" y1=\"122\" x2=\"158\" y2=\"122\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"74\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">tanks (x)</text><g transform=\"translate(206.0 40.0) rotate(0) scale(0.9)\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polygon points=\"12,0 5,-2.2 -9,-1.6 -9,1.6 5,2.2\"/><polygon points=\"3,0 -4,-10 -7,-10 -3,0 -7,10 -4,10\"/><polygon points=\"-8,0 -11,-4.5 -12.5,-4.5 -10.5,0 -12.5,4.5 -11,4.5\"/></g><text x=\"198.43\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">fuel budget \u03a3 = 1</text><text x=\"202.72\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">keep max(0, x\u1d62 \u2212 \u03c4)</text><text x=\"202.72\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c4 = 1.5/2 = 0.75</text><text x=\"198.1648\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">p = (.75, .25, 0, 0)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Pour the tanks x into a budget \u03a3 = 1: lower a common level \u03c4 until what sticks out above it sums to 1. Here \u03c4 = (2.5 \u2212 1)/2 = 0.75, and p = max(0, x \u2212 \u03c41) = (0.75, 0.25, 0, 0).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Problem:</strong> project $x=(1.5,\\,1.0,\\,0.2,\\,-0.3)$ onto the simplex $\\{p\\ge0,\\ \\sum p_i=1\\}$. The answer has the form $p_i=\\max(0,\\,x_i-\\tau)$ for a single threshold $\\tau$ with $\\sum p_i=1$.",
      "<strong>Find $\\tau$:</strong> sort descending ($1.5,1.0,0.2,-0.3$). For $k$ active coordinates try $\\tau_k=\\frac{(\\text{sum of top }k)-1}{k}$: $\\tau_1=0.5$, $\\tau_2=\\frac{2.5-1}{2}=0.75$, $\\tau_3=\\frac{2.7-1}{3}\\approx0.57$. Keep the largest $k$ with $x_{(k)}>\\tau_k$: $1.0>0.75$ \u2713 but $0.2>0.57$ \u2717, so $k=2$, $\\tau=0.75$.",
      "<strong>Result:</strong> $p=(1.5-0.75,\\ 1.0-0.75,\\ 0,\\ 0)=(0.75,\\ 0.25,\\ 0,\\ 0)$. Check: $p\\ge0$ and $\\sum p=1$ \u2713."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\Pi_\\Delta(x)=\\max(0,\\,x-\\tau\\mathbf 1),\\quad \\tau=\\frac{\\sum_{i\\le k}x_{(i)}-1}{k}=\\frac{2.5-1}{2}=0.75\\ \\Rightarrow\\ p=(0.75,\\,0.25,\\,0,\\,0)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The airplane analogy.</strong> A fixed fuel budget (total exactly 1) shared among tanks. Shave one common level $\\tau$ off every tank reading, clipping at empty: the tanks that stay above the level keep their excess, the rest go dry, and $\\tau$ is chosen so the leftover fuel sums to 1. That is the simplex projection.",
    "examTrap": "Do not just clip negatives and divide by the sum: that gives (1.5, 1.0, 0.2, 0)/2.7 = (0.56, 0.37, 0.07, 0), which is NOT the Euclidean projection. The threshold \u03c4 must be subtracted first. Sorting makes it O(n log n); a median-finding method gets O(n).",
    "hint": "How do you find the water level $\\tau$ that makes the leftover fuel sum to one?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$x-\\tau\\mathbf1$ shaves the same level off every tank;</strong> $\\max(0,\\cdot)$ lets empty tanks stay empty.",
      "<strong>$\\tau=\\frac{\\sum_{i\\le k}x_{(i)}-1}{k}$:</strong> the extra over 1 in the $k$ largest tanks, shared equally ($\\frac{2.5-1}{2}=0.75$).",
      "<strong>Result $(0.75,0.25,0,0)$ sums to 1 and is the nearest point of the simplex.</strong>"
    ],
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "Projection onto the simplex $\\Delta=\\{x\\ge0,\\ \\mathbf 1^\\top x=1\\}$: $P_\\Delta(p)_i=\\max\\{p_i-\\tau,0\\}$, where $\\tau$ is chosen so that $\\sum_i\\max\\{p_i-\\tau,0\\}=1$.",
