    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-1405\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"112.0\" cy=\"84.0\" r=\"46.0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><g transform=\"translate(112.0 38.0) rotate(0) scale(0.8)\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polygon points=\"12,0 5,-2.2 -9,-1.6 -9,1.6 5,2.2\"/><polygon points=\"3,0 -4,-10 -7,-10 -3,0 -7,10 -4,10\"/><polygon points=\"-8,0 -11,-4.5 -12.5,-4.5 -10.5,0 -12.5,4.5 -11,4.5\"/></g><circle cx=\"112.0\" cy=\"38.0\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"108\" y=\"29\" font-size=\"9.5\" font-family=\"serif\" font-style=\"italic\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2096</text><line x1=\"126.0\" y1=\"36.0\" x2=\"165.0\" y2=\"36.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-1405)\"/><circle cx=\"168.0\" cy=\"36.0\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"174\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"serif\" font-style=\"italic\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">y = x\u2096 \u2212 \u03b1P\u2096\u2207f</text><line x1=\"168.0\" y1=\"36.0\" x2=\"148.9\" y2=\"53.1\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-1405)\"/><circle cx=\"146.9\" cy=\"54.1\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"153.9\" y=\"64.1\" font-size=\"9.5\" font-family=\"serif\" font-style=\"italic\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2096\u208a\u2081</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">h(x) = 0</text><text x=\"28.0\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">restore: y \u2212 \u2207h\u1d40(\u2207h\u2207h\u1d40)\u207b\u00b9h(y) lands on h = 0</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Fly a tangent step y = x\u2096 \u2212 \u03b1P\u2096\u2207f(x\u2096); on a curved surface h(x) = 0 it leaves the surface. The restoration step x\u2096\u208a\u2081 = y \u2212 \u2207h(y)\u1d40(\u2207h(y)\u2207h(y)\u1d40)\u207b\u00b9h(y) drops it back onto the surface.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>What:</strong> on a curved constraint surface $h(x)=0$ a step along the tangent plane lands slightly off the surface, so each iteration is a <em>tangent step</em> followed by a <em>restoration step</em>.",
      "<strong>How:</strong> (1) tangent step $y=x_k-\\alpha P_k\\nabla f(x_k)$ with $P_k$ the projector onto the tangent plane; (2) restoration: Newton-correct $y$ back to feasibility along the normal: $x_{k+1}=y-\\nabla h\\,[\\nabla h^\\top\\nabla h]^{-1}h(y)$.",
      "<strong>Why it matters:</strong> this is how gradient projection extends from simple sets to nonlinear equality constraints. If $\\alpha$ is too large, $y$ is too far from the surface and restoration may fail or land on a different branch."
    ],
    "math": "$$y=x_k-\\alpha P_k\\nabla f(x_k),\\qquad x_{k+1}=y-\\nabla h(y)^\\top\\big(\\nabla h(y)\\nabla h(y)^\\top\\big)^{-1}h(y)\\quad(\\text{restoration})$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The airplane analogy.</strong> On a curved boundary (a banked runway), flying straight ahead along the tangent takes you off the surface. Restoration is the fix: descend along the normal to put your wheels back on the curved surface before the next hop.",
    "examTrap": "If step size $\\alpha$ is chosen too large, the tangent point $y$ may fly so far from the manifold that the Newton restoration phase fails to converge (or converges to a completely different branch of the constraint surface)!",
    "hint": "How does the pilot get back onto a curved runway after a straight step?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$y=x_k-\\alpha P_k\\nabla f(x_k)$:</strong> project gravity onto the tangent plane so you slide along the wall (nose $P_k\\nabla f$).",
      "<strong>The straight step leaves the curved surface,</strong> so $h(y)\\ne0$ measures how far off you are.",
      "<strong>$-\\nabla h(y)^\\top(\\nabla h(y)\\nabla h(y)^\\top)^{-1}h(y)$ = drop along the normal</strong> by exactly the amount needed to restore $h=0$."
    ],
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "For nonlinear equality constraints $h(x)=0$, a step along the tangent plane leaves the surface; a <b>restoration step</b> returns to it, e.g. $x\\leftarrow x-\\nabla h(x)^\\top\\big(\\nabla h(x)\\nabla h(x)^\\top\\big)^{-1}h(x)$ (Gauss\u2013Newton step on $h(x)=0$).",
