    "title": "Dropping a Constraint with Negative Multiplier",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-1503\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"10\" y=\"104\" width=\"220\" height=\"34\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d1d5db\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><line x1=\"10.0\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"230.0\" y2=\"104.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"16.1\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"16.1\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"28.3\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"28.3\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"40.6\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"40.6\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"52.8\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"52.8\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"65.0\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"65.0\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"77.2\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"77.2\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"89.4\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"89.4\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"101.7\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"101.7\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"113.9\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"113.9\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"126.1\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"126.1\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"138.3\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"138.3\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"150.6\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"150.6\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"162.8\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"162.8\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"175.0\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"175.0\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"187.2\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"187.2\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"199.4\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"199.4\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"211.7\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"211.7\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"223.9\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"223.9\" y2=\"111.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><g transform=\"translate(80.0 92.0) rotate(0) scale(1)\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polygon points=\"12,0 5,-2.2 -9,-1.6 -9,1.6 5,2.2\"/><polygon points=\"3,0 -4,-10 -7,-10 -3,0 -7,10 -4,10\"/><polygon points=\"-8,0 -11,-4.5 -12.5,-4.5 -10.5,0 -12.5,4.5 -11,4.5\"/></g><line x1=\"80.0\" y1=\"82.0\" x2=\"80.0\" y2=\"36.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-1503)\"/><text x=\"86\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"serif\" font-style=\"italic\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">gravity points away</text><text x=\"155.8784\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bb\u0302\u2c7c &lt; 0: the wall</text><text x=\"145.8632\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">would have to pull</text><line x1=\"98.0\" y1=\"88.0\" x2=\"178.0\" y2=\"52.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-1503)\"/><text x=\"232\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">W\u2096\u208a\u2081 = W\u2096 \u2216 {j} \u2197</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "With p\u2096 = 0 you are stuck on the current walls. If some multiplier \u03bb\u0302\u2c7c < 0, that wall would have to pull you back, so gravity points away from it: drop it, W\u2096\u208a\u2081 = W\u2096 \u2216 {j}, and take off.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>What:</strong> when the equality subproblem gives $p_k=0$ you are at the minimum on the current working surface. Now ask: is leaving that surface worthwhile?",
      "<strong>How:</strong> compute the multipliers $\\lambda_i$ of the working constraints. If all $\\lambda_i\\ge0$, the KKT conditions hold and you are done. If some $\\lambda_j\\lt 0$, then $-\\nabla f$ points <em>into</em> the feasible side of wall $j$, so dropping it lets you decrease $f$.",
      "<strong>Why it matters:</strong> drop the constraint with the most negative multiplier. Drop only when $p_k=0$; dropping while $p_k\\ne0$ can cause cycling."
    ],
    "math": "$$p_k=0\\ \\text{ and }\\ \\hat\\lambda_j=\\min_{i\\in W_k}\\hat\\lambda_i\\lt0\\implies W_{k+1}=W_k\\setminus\\{j\\}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The airplane analogy.</strong> Parked against a wall, the force calculation says the wall would have to pull you (a negative multiplier). Walls cannot pull, so gravity actually wants you off that wall: release the brakes, drop that wall from the working set and take off away from it.",
    "examTrap": "You can ONLY drop a constraint when $p_k = 0$ (at a stationary point of the current working surface)! Dropping a constraint while $p_k \\ne 0$ can cause premature release and severe algorithmic cycling.",
    "hint": "When does the pilot release a wall, and which one?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$p_k=0$:</strong> sliding along the current walls goes nowhere, you are at the lowest point of that runway.",
      "<strong>$\\hat\\lambda_j\\lt0$:</strong> that wall would have to pull, which walls cannot do: gravity actually wants you off it.",
      "<strong>Drop the most negative $\\hat\\lambda_j$</strong> and the next step leaves that wall and gains altitude."
    ],
    "stmtKind": "PROPOSITION",
    "statement": "If $p_k=0$, compute the multipliers $\\hat\\lambda_i$ of the equality QP. If all $\\hat\\lambda_i\\ge0$ for inequality constraints in $W_k$, $x_k$ is optimal (KKT holds); otherwise remove a constraint with $\\hat\\lambda_j\\lt 0$ (usually the most negative) from $W_k$.",
    "textbookImg": null,
