    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-1504\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"14\" y=\"24\" width=\"50\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"39\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">W\u2080  f\u2080</text><line x1=\"66.0\" y1=\"35.0\" x2=\"64.0\" y2=\"63.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-1504)\"/><rect x=\"66\" y=\"52\" width=\"50\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"91\" y=\"67\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">W\u2081  f\u2081</text><line x1=\"118.0\" y1=\"63.0\" x2=\"116.0\" y2=\"91.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-1504)\"/><rect x=\"118\" y=\"80\" width=\"50\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"143\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">W\u2082  f\u2082</text><line x1=\"170.0\" y1=\"91.0\" x2=\"168.0\" y2=\"119.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-1504)\"/><rect x=\"170\" y=\"108\" width=\"50\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"195\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">W\u2083  f\u2083</text><g transform=\"translate(234.0 136.0) rotate(0) scale(0.5)\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polygon points=\"12,0 5,-2.2 -9,-1.6 -9,1.6 5,2.2\"/><polygon points=\"3,0 -4,-10 -7,-10 -3,0 -7,10 -4,10\"/><polygon points=\"-8,0 -11,-4.5 -12.5,-4.5 -10.5,0 -12.5,4.5 -11,4.5\"/></g><text x=\"10\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">G \u227b 0, \u03b1\u2096 > 0 \u21d2</text><text x=\"10\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f\u2080 > f\u2081 > f\u2082 > f\u2083</text><text x=\"10\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">no W repeats \u21d2 \u2264 2\u1d50 steps</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "With G \u227b 0 and every step \u03b1\u2096 > 0, the altitude strictly falls, f\u2080 > f\u2081 > f\u2082 > \u2026. A working set can never come back, and there are at most 2\u1d50 of them, so the method stops in finitely many steps.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>What:</strong> for a strictly convex QP ($G\\succ0$) with no degeneracy (every step length $\\alpha_k\\gt 0$), the active-set method reaches the exact optimum in a finite number of iterations.",
      "<strong>How:</strong> there are at most $2^m$ possible working sets, and each real step (a full step or a move after dropping a constraint) strictly lowers $f$. So no working set can ever be visited twice.",
      "<strong>Why it matters:</strong> it is an <em>exact</em> method: no tolerance, no infinite convergence. The one danger is degeneracy, where a zero-length step leaves $f$ unchanged."
    ],
    "math": "$$G\\succ0\\ \\text{ and }\\ \\alpha_k\\gt0\\implies f(x_{k+1})\\lt f(x_k)\\implies\\text{terminates in}\\le2^m\\text{ steps}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The airplane analogy.</strong> Every hop either hits a new wall or lands at the lowest point of the current runway, and every hop lowers altitude, so you never return to a working set you already used. There are only finitely many wall subsets, so the flight must finish in finitely many hops.",
    "examTrap": "Finite termination strictly requires <strong>non-degeneracy</strong>! If $\\alpha_k = 0$ (a degenerate vertex where multiple constraints intersect), $f(x)$ does not decrease, which opens the possibility of infinite cycling.",
    "hint": "Why does the flight always end in finitely many hops?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$G\\succ0$ and $\\alpha_k\\gt0$:</strong> every real hop strictly lowers the altitude.",
      "<strong>So no working set ever repeats,</strong> because a repeat would mean the same altitude twice.",
      "<strong>There are only $2^m$ possible working sets,</strong> hence at most $2^m$ hops."
    ],
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "If $G\\succ0$ and every step with $\\alpha_k\\gt 0$ strictly decreases the objective, the active-set method terminates in finitely many iterations, since no working set can recur and there are finitely many working sets.",
