    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-1905\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"206.0\" y1=\"10.0\" x2=\"206.0\" y2=\"134.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"206.0\" y1=\"15.6\" x2=\"213.0\" y2=\"15.6\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"206.0\" y1=\"26.9\" x2=\"213.0\" y2=\"26.9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"206.0\" y1=\"38.2\" x2=\"213.0\" y2=\"38.2\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"206.0\" y1=\"49.5\" x2=\"213.0\" y2=\"49.5\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"206.0\" y1=\"60.7\" x2=\"213.0\" y2=\"60.7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"206.0\" y1=\"72.0\" x2=\"213.0\" y2=\"72.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"206.0\" y1=\"83.3\" x2=\"213.0\" y2=\"83.3\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"206.0\" y1=\"94.5\" x2=\"213.0\" y2=\"94.5\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"206.0\" y1=\"105.8\" x2=\"213.0\" y2=\"105.8\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"206.0\" y1=\"117.1\" x2=\"213.0\" y2=\"117.1\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"206.0\" y1=\"128.4\" x2=\"213.0\" y2=\"128.4\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"204\" y2=\"44\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 3\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"204\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 3\"/><circle cx=\"30.0\" cy=\"44.0\" r=\"2.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"100.0\" cy=\"44.0\" r=\"2.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"148.0\" cy=\"44.0\" r=\"2.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"172.0\" cy=\"44.0\" r=\"2.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"186.0\" cy=\"44.0\" r=\"2.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"194.0\" cy=\"44.0\" r=\"2.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">penalty: creeps toward the wall, never lands</text><circle cx=\"30.0\" cy=\"100.0\" r=\"2.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"120.0\" cy=\"100.0\" r=\"2.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"206.0\" cy=\"100.0\" r=\"2.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><g transform=\"translate(160.0 86.0) rotate(0) scale(0.55)\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polygon points=\"12,0 5,-2.2 -9,-1.6 -9,1.6 5,2.2\"/><polygon points=\"3,0 -4,-10 -7,-10 -3,0 -7,10 -4,10\"/><polygon points=\"-8,0 -11,-4.5 -12.5,-4.5 -10.5,0 -12.5,4.5 -11,4.5\"/></g><text x=\"110\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">augmented: \u03bb\u2096\u208a\u2081 = \u03bb\u2096 + c\u2096h(x\u2096)</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">lands exactly with a moderate c</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Pure penalty creeps toward the wall but never lands. The augmented Lagrangian also adjusts the multiplier after each solve, \u03bb\u2096\u208a\u2081 = \u03bb\u2096 + c\u2096h(x\u2096), and lands exactly on the wall with only a moderate fine c.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>What:</strong> the augmented Lagrangian $\\mathcal{L}_c(x,\\lambda)=f+\\lambda^Th+\\tfrac c2\\|h\\|^2$ (Hestenes\u2013Powell) adds a multiplier term to the quadratic penalty.",
      "<strong>How:</strong> alternate (1) minimize $\\mathcal{L}_c(x,\\lambda_k)$ over $x$; (2) update the multiplier by $\\lambda_{k+1}=\\lambda_k+c\\,h(x_k)$ (gradient <em>ascent</em> on the dual, with a plus sign).",
      "<strong>Why it matters:</strong> the multiplier does most of the work of balancing $-\\nabla f$, so $c$ only has to be large enough to make $\\mathcal{L}_c$ locally convex, a <em>finite</em> value. No $c\\to\\infty$ means no ill-conditioning."
    ],
    "math": "$$L_c(x,\\lambda)=f(x)+\\lambda^\\top h(x)+\\tfrac c2\\|h(x)\\|^2;\\quad x_k\\in\\arg\\min_xL_{c_k}(x,\\lambda_k),\\ \\ \\lambda_{k+1}=\\lambda_k+c_kh(x_k)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The airplane analogy.</strong> Ordinary penalty needs the fine to grow forever ($c\\to\\infty$). The augmented Lagrangian lets the tower also adjust a standing reservation $\\lambda$ so that the plane lands exactly on the boundary with only a moderate fine.",
    "examTrap": "The multiplier update is $\\lambda_{k+1} = \\lambda_k + c_k h(x_k)$ (NOT minus!). Because $h(x) = \\nabla_\\lambda \\mathcal{L}_c$ is the exact gradient of the dual function with respect to $\\lambda$, this update is pure gradient ascent on the dual.",
    "hint": "What does the tower adjust so the fine does not have to grow forever?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$h(x_k)$ = remaining violation after the current hop.</strong>",
      "<strong>$c_kh(x_k)$ = the correction the multiplier needs:</strong> the same force-from-depth reading as penalty recovery.",
      "<strong>$\\lambda_{k+1}=\\lambda_k+c_kh(x_k)$</strong> converges without sending $c_k\\to\\infty$, so the problem stays well conditioned."
    ],
    "stmtKind": "ALGORITHM",
    "statement": "<b>Augmented Lagrangian (method of multipliers).</b> $L_c(x,\\lambda)=f(x)+\\lambda^\\top h(x)+\\tfrac c2\\|h(x)\\|^2$. Repeat: $x_k\\in\\arg\\min_xL_{c_k}(x,\\lambda_k)$; $\\lambda_{k+1}=\\lambda_k+c_kh(x_k)$. Convergence holds for finite (moderately large) $c$, avoiding the ill-conditioning of $c\\to\\infty$.",
