    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-20101\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><polygon points=\"12,126 144,126 192,66 60,66\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">U (through the pin)</text><polygon points=\"100,56 214,56 234,22 120,22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">W: the same sheet, shifted</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">0 \u2209 W \u2717 not a subspace</text><circle cx=\"64.0\" cy=\"96.0\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"64.0\" cy=\"96.0\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">0 \u2208 U \u2713</text><line x1=\"64.0\" y1=\"96.0\" x2=\"110.0\" y2=\"112.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-20101)\"/><text x=\"113\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">u</text><line x1=\"64.0\" y1=\"96.0\" x2=\"94.0\" y2=\"74.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-20101)\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">v</text><line x1=\"110.0\" y1=\"112.0\" x2=\"140.0\" y2=\"90.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"94.0\" y1=\"74.0\" x2=\"140.0\" y2=\"90.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"64.0\" y1=\"96.0\" x2=\"140.0\" y2=\"90.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-20101)\"/><text x=\"145\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03b1u + \u03b2v \u2208 U \u2713</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">U \u2264 V \u21d4 0 \u2208 U and \u03b1u + \u03b2v \u2208 U</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The shaded sheet U goes through the centre pin 0, and any mix \u03b1u + \u03b2v of two of its arrows stays in it. The dashed sheet W is shifted off the pin, so 0 \u2209 W and it fails.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "A subset $U \\subset V$ of a vector space over field $\\mathbb{F}$ is a <strong>Subspace</strong> if and only if it satisfies the <strong>3-Step Test</strong>:",
      "<strong>1. Additive Identity:</strong> $0 \\in U$. (If the origin is missing, $U$ fails immediately).",
      "<strong>2. Closure under Addition:</strong> $u, v \\in U \\implies u + v \\in U$. <strong>3. Closure under Scalar Mult:</strong> $u \\in U, c \\in \\mathbb{F} \\implies c u \\in U$."
    ],
    "math": "$$U \\le V \\iff 0 \\in U \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\alpha u + \\beta v \\in U \\quad \\forall \\, u, v \\in U, \\; \\alpha, \\beta \\in \\mathbb{F}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A sheet through the pin.</strong> Put your fingers on the photo and drag: every arrow starts at the centre pin. A flat sheet through the pin is a subspace, because any mix of two of its arrows stays in the sheet. Slide the sheet off the pin and the zero arrow is no longer in it.",
    "examTrap": "Testing if an affine plane (e.g. $W = \\{(x, y, z) : x + 2y - z = 4\\}$) is a subspace. Answer: NO! $(0,0,0) \\notin W$. It is an affine manifold, not a linear subspace.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Subspace.</b> A subset $U$ of a vector space $V$ over $\\mathbb F$ is a subspace of $V$ if $U$ is itself a vector space with the same addition and scalar multiplication. Equivalently (Axler 1.34): $0\\in U$; $u,w\\in U\\Rightarrow u+w\\in U$; and $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb F,\\ u\\in U\\Rightarrow\\lambda u\\in U$.",
    "hint": "Which three checks does a set of arrows need before it counts as a subspace?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$0\\in U$ = the set contains the pin itself.</strong> The zero arrow (no movement) must be in it; a sheet that misses the pin fails at once.",
      "<strong>$\\alpha u+\\beta v\\in U$ = mixing arrows keeps you inside.</strong> Stretch $u$, stretch $v$, add them tip to tail: still in $U$. This is closure under addition and scaling in one line.",
      "<strong>Why only these:</strong> the other vector-space rules (associativity, distributivity) are inherited from $V$, so these are the only things that can break."
    ],
    "textbookImg": null,
