    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-20102\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"10\" y=\"6\" width=\"220\" height=\"134\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"112.0\" y1=\"136\" x2=\"128.0\" y2=\"136\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"18\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"222\" y2=\"84\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"222\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">U\u2081</text><line x1=\"64\" y1=\"136\" x2=\"162\" y2=\"12\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"166\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">U\u2082</text><circle cx=\"110.0\" cy=\"84.0\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"110.0\" cy=\"84.0\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"116\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">U\u2081 \u2229 U\u2082 = {0}</text><line x1=\"110.0\" y1=\"84.0\" x2=\"170.0\" y2=\"84.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-20102)\"/><text x=\"156\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">u\u2081</text><line x1=\"110.0\" y1=\"84.0\" x2=\"134.0\" y2=\"54.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-20102)\"/><text x=\"128\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">u\u2082</text><line x1=\"170.0\" y1=\"84.0\" x2=\"194.0\" y2=\"54.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"134.0\" y1=\"54.0\" x2=\"194.0\" y2=\"54.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"110.0\" y1=\"84.0\" x2=\"194.0\" y2=\"54.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-20102)\"/><text x=\"194\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">v = u\u2081 + u\u2082</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">only one way to split v</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u21d2 U\u2081 + U\u2082 = U\u2081 \u2295 U\u2082</text></svg>",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "The <strong>Sum of Subspaces</strong> is $U_1 + \\dots + U_m = \\{u_1 + \\dots + u_m : u_i \\in U_i\\}$. It is the smallest subspace containing all $U_i$.",
      "The sum is called a <strong>Direct Sum</strong>, written $U_1 \\oplus \\dots \\oplus U_m$, if every vector $v \\in U_1 + \\dots + U_m$ can be written as $v = u_1 + \\dots + u_m$ in <strong>EXACTLY ONE UNIQUE WAY</strong>.",
      "<strong>Two Subspaces ($m = 2$):</strong> The sum $U_1 + U_2$ is direct if and only if their intersection is trivial: $U_1 \\cap U_2 = \\{0\\}$."
    ],
    "math": "$$U_1 + U_2 = U_1 \\oplus U_2 \\iff U_1 \\cap U_2 = \\{\\mathbf{0}\\}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Swipe right, swipe up.</strong> Every drag on the photo is some amount sideways plus some amount up, and there is only one way to say it, because the sideways line and the up line meet only at the pin.",
    "examTrap": "The intersection condition $U_i \\cap U_j = \\{0\\}$ ONLY works for $m=2$ subspaces! For 3 or more subspaces, pairwise trivial intersection does NOT guarantee a direct sum.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Sum and direct sum.</b> For subspaces $U_1,\\dots,U_m$ of $V$, $U_1+\\dots+U_m=\\{u_1+\\dots+u_m: u_i\\in U_i\\}$. The sum is a direct sum, written $U_1\\oplus\\dots\\oplus U_m$, if each element of it can be written in only one way as $u_1+\\dots+u_m$ with $u_i\\in U_i$. For two subspaces (Axler 1.46): $U_1+U_2$ is direct $\\iff U_1\\cap U_2=\\{0\\}$.",
    "hint": "When can every arrow be split into a U\u2081 part and a U\u2082 part in exactly one way?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$U_1+U_2$ = every arrow you can build</strong> by adding an arrow along $U_1$ to an arrow along $U_2$.",
      "<strong>$U_1\\oplus U_2$ = the split is unique.</strong> Each arrow $v$ has only one pair $(u_1,u_2)$.",
      "<strong>$U_1\\cap U_2=\\{0\\}$ = the two lines share only the pin.</strong> If they shared a direction, you could move some of it from one part to the other and get a second split."
    ]
