    "title": "Fundamental Direct Sum Zero-Vector Criterion",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-20103\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">can three arrows cancel back to the pin?</text><circle cx=\"120.0\" cy=\"80.0\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"120.0\" cy=\"80.0\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><line x1=\"120.0\" y1=\"80.0\" x2=\"60.0\" y2=\"58.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-20103)\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">u\u2081 \u2208 U\u2081</text><line x1=\"120.0\" y1=\"80.0\" x2=\"176.0\" y2=\"48.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-20103)\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">u\u2082 \u2208 U\u2082</text><line x1=\"120.0\" y1=\"80.0\" x2=\"128.0\" y2=\"124.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-20103)\"/><text x=\"134\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">u\u2083 \u2208 U\u2083</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">u\u2081 + u\u2082 + u\u2083 = 0</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u21d2 u\u2081 = u\u2082 = u\u2083 = 0 ?</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">only with all zero \u21d4 the sum is direct</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Three arrows u\u2081, u\u2082, u\u2083 from three subspaces. The sum is direct exactly when u\u2081 + u\u2082 + u\u2083 = 0 forces u\u2081 = u\u2082 = u\u2083 = 0.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Master Theorem (Axler 1.44):</strong> The sum $U_1 + \\dots + U_m$ is a direct sum if and only if the only way to write the zero vector as a sum $u_1 + \\dots + u_m = 0$ (with $u_i \\in U_i$) is: $u_1 = u_2 = \\dots = u_m = 0$.",
      "<strong>Proof $(\\implies)$:</strong> If the sum is direct, representation of 0 is unique. Since $0 + \\dots + 0 = 0$, this must be the only representation.",
      "<strong>Proof $(\\impliedby)$:</strong> If $v = u_1 + \\dots + u_m = w_1 + \\dots + w_m$, subtracting gives $(u_1 - w_1) + \\dots + (u_m - w_m) = 0$. By hypothesis, each $u_i - w_i = 0 \\implies u_i = w_i$."
    ],
    "math": "$$U_1 \\oplus \\dots \\oplus U_m \\iff \\left( \\sum_{i=1}^m u_i = 0, \\; u_i \\in U_i \\implies u_1 = \\dots = u_m = 0 \\right)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Three drags that undo each other.</strong> If you can drag the photo along three different lines and end exactly where you started, the lines are tangled and the sum is not direct. A direct sum means the only way back is to not drag at all.",
    "examTrap": "Always use the zero-vector criterion when testing 3 or more subspaces! It is universal, completely immune to pairwise intersection traps, and matches the definition of linear independence.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Condition for a direct sum (Axler 1.45).</b> Let $U_1,\\dots,U_m$ be subspaces of $V$. Then $U_1+\\dots+U_m$ is a direct sum if and only if the only way to write $0$ as $u_1+\\dots+u_m$, with each $u_i\\in U_i$, is by taking every $u_i=0$.",
    "hint": "Instead of checking every arrow, which single arrow is enough to test?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\sum u_i=0$ with $u_i\\in U_i$</strong> = arrows from different subspaces that, added tip to tail, bring you back to the pin.",
      "<strong>$\\Rightarrow u_1=\\dots=u_m=0$</strong> = the only way back to the pin is to not move at all. Then 0 has one representation.",
      "<strong>Why 0 is enough:</strong> two splits of the same $v$ subtract to a split of 0, so uniqueness at 0 gives uniqueness everywhere."
    ],
