    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-20105\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"72\" rx=\"58\" ry=\"40\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" transform=\"rotate(0 92 72)\"/><ellipse cx=\"148\" cy=\"72\" rx=\"58\" ry=\"40\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" transform=\"rotate(0 148 72)\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">dim U\u2081</text><text x=\"186\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">dim U\u2082</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">dim</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">U\u2081 \u2229 U\u2082</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">count the shared directions once</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">dim(U\u2081 + U\u2082) = dim U\u2081 + dim U\u2082 \u2212 dim(U\u2081 \u2229 U\u2082)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">two sheets in \u211d\u00b3: 2 + 2 \u2212 3 \u2265 1 \u21d2 they share a line</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Subspaces U\u2081 and U\u2082 overlap in U\u2081 \u2229 U\u2082. dim(U\u2081 + U\u2082) = dim U\u2081 + dim U\u2082 \u2212 dim(U\u2081 \u2229 U\u2082): the shared directions are counted once.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Theorem:</strong> For finite-dimensional subspaces $U_1, U_2 \\le V$: $\\dim(U_1 + U_2) = \\dim U_1 + \\dim U_2 - \\dim(U_1 \\cap U_2)$.",
      "<strong>Direct Sum Characterization:</strong> The sum is direct ($U_1 \\oplus U_2$) if and only if $\\dim(U_1 \\cap U_2) = 0$, which yields the additive formula: $\\dim(U_1 \\oplus U_2) = \\dim U_1 + \\dim U_2$.",
      "<strong>Proof Mechanism:</strong> Start with basis $\\{v_1, \\dots, v_k\\}$ of $U_1 \\cap U_2$. Extend to basis of $U_1$ and basis of $U_2$. The union of these extended bases forms a basis of $U_1 + U_2$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\dim(U_1 + U_2) = \\dim U_1 + \\dim U_2 - \\dim(U_1 \\cap U_2) \\le \\dim U_1 + \\dim U_2$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Two editing sliders that overlap.</strong> One tool moves the photo left\u2013right and up\u2013down, another moves it up\u2013down and in\u2013out. Together they give 3 directions, not 4: the shared up\u2013down is counted once.",
    "examTrap": "If $\\dim(U_1) + \\dim(U_2) > \\dim(V)$, the subspaces MUST have a non-trivial intersection! E.g., two 2D planes in $\\mathbb{R}^3$ must intersect in at least a line: $\\dim(U_1 \\cap U_2) \\ge 2 + 2 - 3 = 1$.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Dimension of a sum (Axler 2.43).</b> If $V_1$ and $V_2$ are subspaces of a finite-dimensional vector space, then $\\dim(V_1+V_2)=\\dim V_1+\\dim V_2-\\dim(V_1\\cap V_2)$. In particular, the sum is direct $\\iff\\dim(V_1+V_2)=\\dim V_1+\\dim V_2$.",
    "hint": "Two subspaces share some directions. How many independent directions does their sum really have?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\dim U_1+\\dim U_2$</strong> = add up the independent directions of each subspace.",
      "<strong>$-\\dim(U_1\\cap U_2)$</strong> = the shared directions were counted twice, so remove them once (like $|A\\cup B|=|A|+|B|-|A\\cap B|$).",
      "<strong>Consequence:</strong> if $\\dim U_1+\\dim U_2>\\dim V$ they must share a direction, e.g. two planes in $\\mathbb R^3$ share at least a line."
    ],
