    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-20106\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"8\" y=\"44\" width=\"46\" height=\"46\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"31\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">A</text><text x=\"31\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">any edit</text><text x=\"31\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">matrix</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">=</text><rect x=\"72\" y=\"44\" width=\"66\" height=\"46\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">(A + A\u1d40)/2</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2208 \ud835\udcae\u2099</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">pure stretch:</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">S\u1d40 = S</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">+</text><rect x=\"156\" y=\"44\" width=\"76\" height=\"46\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"194\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">(A \u2212 A\u1d40)/2</text><text x=\"194\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2208 \ud835\udc9c\u2099</text><text x=\"194\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">pure spin:</text><text x=\"194\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">K\u1d40 = \u2212K</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">M\u2099 = \ud835\udcae\u2099 \u2295 \ud835\udc9c\u2099</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udcae\u2099 \u2229 \ud835\udc9c\u2099: A\u1d40 = A = \u2212A \u21d2 A = 0</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Any matrix A splits as (A + A\u1d40)/2 in \ud835\udcae\u2099 (stretch) plus (A \u2212 A\u1d40)/2 in \ud835\udc9c\u2099 (spin), and \ud835\udcae\u2099 \u2229 \ud835\udc9c\u2099 = {0}, so M\u2099 = \ud835\udcae\u2099 \u2295 \ud835\udc9c\u2099.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Problem:</strong> Prove $M_{n \\times n}(\\mathbb{R}) = \\mathcal{S}_n \\oplus \\mathcal{A}_n$, where $\\mathcal{S}_n = \\{A : A^T = A\\}$ and $\\mathcal{A}_n = \\{A : A^T = -A\\}$.",
      "<strong>Step 1 (Existence):</strong> For any $A \\in M_{n \\times n}$, write: $A = \\frac{A + A^T}{2} + \\frac{A - A^T}{2}$. $\\frac{A + A^T}{2} \\in \\mathcal{S}_n$ and $\\frac{A - A^T}{2} \\in \\mathcal{A}_n$. Thus $M_{n \\times n} = \\mathcal{S}_n + \\mathcal{A}_n$.",
      "<strong>Step 2 (Uniqueness / Intersection):</strong> Let $A \\in \\mathcal{S}_n \\cap \\mathcal{A}_n$. Then $A^T = A$ and $A^T = -A \\implies A = -A \\implies 2A = 0 \\implies A = 0$. Hence $\\mathcal{S}_n \\cap \\mathcal{A}_n = \\{0\\}$, proving direct sum!"
    ],
    "math": "$$A = \\underbrace{\\frac{A + A^T}{2}}_{\\in \\mathcal{S}_n} + \\underbrace{\\frac{A - A^T}{2}}_{\\in \\mathcal{A}_n}, \\quad \\mathcal{S}_n \\cap \\mathcal{A}_n = \\{0\\} \\implies M_n = \\mathcal{S}_n \\oplus \\mathcal{A}_n$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Stretch plus spin.</strong> Any small edit you make with two fingers is part stretch (pull the fingers apart along some axes) and part spin (twist them). A move that is both a pure stretch and a pure spin is no move at all.",
    "examTrap": "Check the dimensions: $\\dim \\mathcal{S}_n = \\frac{n(n+1)}{2}$, $\\dim \\mathcal{A}_n = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}$. Their sum is $\\frac{n(n+1)}{2} + \\frac{n(n-1)}{2} = n^2 = \\dim M_{n \\times n}$, confirming the direct sum dimension theorem.",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Claim.</b> $M_{n\\times n}(\\mathbb R)=\\mathcal S_n\\oplus\\mathcal A_n$, where $\\mathcal S_n=\\{A:A^\\top=A\\}$ and $\\mathcal A_n=\\{A:A^\\top=-A\\}$. Proof: $A=\\tfrac12(A+A^\\top)+\\tfrac12(A-A^\\top)$ gives the sum, and $A\\in\\mathcal S_n\\cap\\mathcal A_n\\Rightarrow A=-A\\Rightarrow A=0$ gives directness. Also $\\dim\\mathcal S_n+\\dim\\mathcal A_n=\\tfrac{n(n+1)}2+\\tfrac{n(n-1)}2=n^2$.",
    "hint": "How does any photo edit matrix split into a pure-stretch part and a pure-spin part?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\tfrac12(A+A^\\top)\\in\\mathcal S_n$</strong> = average $A$ with its mirror image: the result equals its own transpose (a stretch along fixed axes).",
      "<strong>$\\tfrac12(A-A^\\top)\\in\\mathcal A_n$</strong> = half the difference: its transpose is its negative (an infinitesimal spin).",
      "<strong>$\\mathcal S_n\\cap\\mathcal A_n=\\{0\\}$</strong> = a matrix that is both has $A=A^\\top=-A$, so it is zero, and the split is unique."
    ],
