    "math": "$$\\mathbb{P}(A) \\ge 0, \\quad \\mathbb{P}(\\Omega) = 1, \\quad \\mathbb{P}\\left(\\bigcup_{i=1}^\\infty A_i\\right) = \\sum_{i=1}^\\infty \\mathbb{P}(A_i) \\; (A_i \\cap A_j = \\emptyset)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Splitting the mornings into cases.</strong> \u201cLate because of rain\u201d, \u201clate because of a breakdown\u201d, \u201clate because I overslept\u201d: no morning is two of these at once, so their chances just add. The third rule says this still works with endlessly many cases.",
