    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Continuity of probability.</b> Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)$ be a probability space. If $A_1\\subset A_2\\subset\\cdots$ in $\\mathcal F$ and $A=\\bigcup_nA_n$ (written $A_n\\uparrow A$), then $\\mathbb P(A)=\\lim_n\\mathbb P(A_n)$. If $B_1\\supset B_2\\supset\\cdots$ in $\\mathcal F$ and $B=\\bigcap_nB_n$ ($B_n\\downarrow B$), then $\\mathbb P(B)=\\lim_n\\mathbb P(B_n)$ (Ross 2.6; Grimmett 1.3).",
