    "id": 40103,
    "subject": "DIP",
    "topicId": "01_Image_Formation_Camera_Geometry_and_Transformations",
    "topicTitle": "01 \u00b7 Image Formation & Transformations",
    "cardNumber": "03",
    "category": "CAMERA INTRINSICS",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-emerald",
    "title": "Intrinsic Calibration Matrix K",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-40103\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"22.0\" width=\"160.0\" height=\"100.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">(0, 0)</text><line x1=\"20.0\" y1=\"22.0\" x2=\"60.0\" y2=\"22.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-40103)\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">u</text><line x1=\"20.0\" y1=\"22.0\" x2=\"20.0\" y2=\"52.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-40103)\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">v</text><line x1=\"94\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"106\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"76\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"104\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">(c\u2093, c\u1d67)</text><line x1=\"100.0\" y1=\"72.0\" x2=\"100.0\" y2=\"122.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"1 3\"/><line x1=\"20.0\" y1=\"72.0\" x2=\"100.0\" y2=\"72.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"1 3\"/><rect x=\"194.0\" y=\"36.0\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"208.0\" y=\"36.0\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"194.0\" y=\"50.0\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"208.0\" y=\"50.0\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"222\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">1 pixel</text><line x1=\"194.0\" y1=\"76.0\" x2=\"222.0\" y2=\"76.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-40103)\"/><text x=\"208\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">1/m\u2093 mm</text><text x=\"194\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f\u2093 = f\u00b7m\u2093</text><text x=\"188.68\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">(pixels per mm</text><text x=\"185.3\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u00d7 focal length)</text><text x=\"100.46000000000001\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">principal point = where the lens axis hits the sensor</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The recorded frame has its origin (0, 0) at the top-left corner and axes u, v. The lens axis hits the principal point (c\u2093, c\u1d67); f\u2093 = f\u00b7m\u2093 is the focal length counted in pixels.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "The upper-triangular <strong>Intrinsic Calibration Matrix $K$</strong> has 5 degrees of freedom:",
      "$$K = \\begin{bmatrix} f_x & s & c_x \\\\ 0 & f_y & c_y \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}$$",
      "<strong>Focal Lengths $f_x, f_y$:</strong> $f_x = f \\cdot m_x, f_y = f \\cdot m_y$, where $m_x, m_y$ are pixels per millimeter. For square pixels, $f_x = f_y$.",
      "<strong>Principal Point $(c_x, c_y)$:</strong> Pixel coordinates where the camera's optical axis pierces the sensor. <strong>Skew $s$:</strong> Non-zero only if sensor axes are not orthogonal (usually $s = 0$)."
    ],
    "math": "$$K = \\begin{bmatrix} f_x & 0 & c_x \\\\ 0 & f_y & c_y \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\quad (5 \\text{ Intrinsic Parameters for General CCD})$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Counting pixels in a 1920\u00d71080 frame.</strong> Pixel (0, 0) is the top-left corner of the recorded frame, so the centre of the lens axis lands near (960, 540). A wider-angle lens has a smaller $f_x$: more street fits across the same pixels.",
    "examTrap": "Never assume the principal point is at $(0, 0)$! In image coordinates, $(0,0)$ is the TOP-LEFT corner of the image. For a $1920 \\times 1080$ sensor, the principal point is approximately $(960, 540)$.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Intrinsic calibration matrix.</b> $K=\\begin{pmatrix}f_x&s&c_x\\\\0&f_y&c_y\\\\0&0&1\\end{pmatrix}$, where $f_x=f\\,m_x$, $f_y=f\\,m_y$ are the focal length in pixels ($m_x,m_y$ pixels per unit length), $(c_x,c_y)$ is the principal point in pixels and $s$ is the skew (zero when sensor axes are orthogonal). $K$ maps a point $(X,Y,Z)$ of the camera frame to the pixel $u=f_xX/Z+c_x,\\ v=f_yY/Z+c_y$ (for $s=0$).",
    "hint": "Where is pixel (0, 0) of the street frame, and where does the lens axis actually land?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$f_x,f_y$ = the focal length counted in pixels.</strong> The real focal length times the number of pixels per millimetre; a square-pixel sensor has $f_x=f_y$.",
      "<strong>$(c_x,c_y)$ = the principal point.</strong> The pixel where the lens axis hits the sensor, about the middle of the frame, not at the corner $(0,0)$.",
      "<strong>$s$ = skew.</strong> Zero unless the pixel rows and columns are not at right angles, which for a modern street camera they are."
    ],
