    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Hierarchy of 2D planar transformations.</b> A homography is $\\mathbf x'\\sim H\\mathbf x$ with $H\\in\\mathbb R^{3\\times3}$ invertible, defined up to scale (8 degrees of freedom). Subgroups: Euclidean $[R\\mid t]$ (3 DOF, preserves lengths and angles); similarity $[sR\\mid t]$ (4, preserves angles); affine, with last row $(0,0,1)$ (6, preserves parallelism); projective (8, preserves straight lines only).",
