    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-40105\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"36\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">output frame</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"22\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2032, y\u2032</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">ask:</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"67\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">where from?</text><line x1=\"40.0\" y1=\"34.0\" x2=\"98.0\" y2=\"52.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-40105)\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">T\u207b\u00b9</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">source frame</text><rect x=\"112.0\" y=\"24.0\" width=\"44\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"134.0\" y=\"48.5\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\"> </text><rect x=\"156.0\" y=\"24.0\" width=\"44\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"178.0\" y=\"48.5\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f\u2081\u2080</text><rect x=\"112.0\" y=\"68.0\" width=\"44\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"134.0\" y=\"92.5\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f\u2080\u2081</text><rect x=\"156.0\" y=\"68.0\" width=\"44\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"178.0\" y=\"92.5\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f\u2081\u2081</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f\u2080\u2080</text><circle cx=\"127.4\" cy=\"50.4\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"131.4\" y=\"60.4\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">x, y</text><line x1=\"127.4\" y1=\"24.0\" x2=\"127.4\" y2=\"50.4\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"112.0\" y1=\"50.4\" x2=\"127.4\" y2=\"50.4\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"119.48\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">a</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"37.2\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">b</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f(x, y) = (1\u2212a)(1\u2212b)f\u2080\u2080 + a(1\u2212b)f\u2081\u2080 + (1\u2212a)b f\u2080\u2081 + ab f\u2081\u2081</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">every output pixel is filled: no holes</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Each pixel (x\u2032, y\u2032) of the corrected frame looks back through T\u207b\u00b9 to a point (x, y) of the camera frame, between four pixels f\u2080\u2080 \u2026 f\u2081\u2081. The offsets a and b give the blend weights.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Forward Mapping:</strong> Iterates over input pixels $(x, y)$, computing destination $(x', y') = T(x, y)$. Since $(x', y')$ are floating-point numbers, rounding causes <strong>holes (unassigned pixels)</strong> and overlap collisions.",
      "<strong>Inverse Mapping (Standard):</strong> Iterates over every discrete destination pixel $(x', y')$, querying source position $(x, y) = T^{-1}(x', y')$.",
      "<strong>Bilinear Interpolation:</strong> Because $(x, y)$ falls between integer coordinates, its intensity is interpolated using a weighted average of its 4 nearest neighbors: $f(x, y) = (1-a)(1-b) f_{00} + a(1-b) f_{10} + (1-a)b f_{01} + ab f_{11}$."
    ],
    "math": "$$I_{\\text{dest}}(x', y') = I_{\\text{src}}(T^{-1}(x', y')) \\quad \\text{via Bilinear 4-Neighbor Interpolation}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Straightening the street frame.</strong> To turn the slanted road into a top-down map, go through the new map pixel by pixel and ask the original frame what colour sits at that spot. Pushing source pixels forward instead leaves little unpainted gaps.",
    "examTrap": "Forward mapping requires expensive splatting algorithms to avoid gaps. All production computer vision and DIP pipelines strictly use INVERSE warping with $T^{-1}$.",
    "stmtKind": "ALGORITHM",
    "statement": "<b>Inverse warping with bilinear interpolation.</b> Given a transformation $T$ and a source image $I_{\\rm src}$, for every integer pixel $(x',y')$ of the output compute $(x,y)=T^{-1}(x',y')$, let $x_0=\\lfloor x\\rfloor$, $y_0=\\lfloor y\\rfloor$, $a=x-x_0$, $b=y-y_0$, and set $I_{\\rm dest}(x',y')=(1-a)(1-b)f_{00}+a(1-b)f_{10}+(1-a)b\\,f_{01}+ab\\,f_{11}$, with $f_{ij}$ the four source pixels around $(x,y)$.",
    "hint": "To fill every pixel of the corrected frame, do you push source pixels forward, or ask each output pixel where it came from?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$T^{-1}(x',y')$ = for each output pixel, ask where it came from.</strong> This visits every output pixel exactly once, so no holes and no double hits (forward mapping has both).",
      "<strong>$(x,y)$ lands between pixels</strong> = the source position is rarely a whole number, so there is no single source pixel to copy.",
      "<strong>$(1-a)(1-b)f_{00}+\\dots$ = blend the four neighbours</strong> by how close the point is to each: the nearer pixel gets the larger weight."
    ],
